    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >One of the world's most beloved literary characters...</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >...is now YOUR problem.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >----</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Hearth &amp; Holmes</strong> is a mystery-solving game set on a backdrop of cozy life simulation. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You play as John Watson, new to his friendship with Sherlock Holmes and desperately trying to cajole his reckless, work-obsessed friend into exercising some level of self-care.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Accompany Holmes through the formative years of his development as a detective:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Should he focus on his <strong>Chemistry </strong>experiments or on learning the <strong>Criminal History</strong> of London?</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Should he hone his skills in <strong>Disguise </strong>or in <strong>Deduction</strong>?</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Or should he abandon all other subjects and respond to every challenge he encounters by playing the <strong>Violin </strong>at it?</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore life at 221B Baker Street:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Finish writing 'A Study in Scarlet' and try to get it published.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Plot with Mrs. Hudson to make sure Holmes eats breakfast.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Apologize to Irene Norton for pretending to set her house on fire.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Play bridge with Professor Moriarty, who is an innocent college professor and certainly doesn't have any nefarious designs on your friend.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Confront darker matters: Holmes' substance abuse and your own PTSD from the Anglo-Afghan War.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >One of the world's most beloved literary characters...</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >...is now YOUR problem.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >----</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Hearth &amp; Holmes</strong> is a mystery-solving game set on a backdrop of cozy life simulation. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You play as John Watson, new to his friendship with Sherlock Holmes and desperately trying to cajole his reckless, work-obsessed friend into exercising some level of self-care.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Accompany Holmes through the formative years of his development as a detective:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Should he focus on his <strong>Chemistry </strong>experiments or on learning the <strong>Criminal History</strong> of London?</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Should he hone his skills in <strong>Disguise </strong>or in <strong>Deduction</strong>?</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Or should he abandon all other subjects and respond to every challenge he encounters by playing the <strong>Violin </strong>at it?</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore life at 221B Baker Street:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Finish writing 'A Study in Scarlet' and try to get it published.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Plot with Mrs. Hudson to make sure Holmes eats breakfast.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Apologize to Irene Norton for pretending to set her house on fire.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Play bridge with Professor Moriarty, who is an innocent college professor and certainly doesn't have any nefarious designs on your friend.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Confront darker matters: Holmes' substance abuse and your own PTSD from the Anglo-Afghan War.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
